    "problem_statement": "Levenshtein distance calculation returns incorrect results\n\n#### Description\n\nThe Levenshtein distance algorithm is producing incorrect distance values for string comparisons. When comparing strings like \"test\" and \"text\", it should return 1 (one character substitution), but it's returning unexpected values.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport textdistance\n\n# Basic test cases that should work\nresult1 = textdistance.levenshtein(\"test\", \"text\")\nprint(f\"Distance between 'test' and 'text': {result1}\")  # Expected: 1\n\nresult2 = textdistance.levenshtein(\"test\", \"tset\") \nprint(f\"Distance between 'test' and 'tset': {result2}\")  # Expected: 2\n\nresult3 = textdistance.levenshtein(\"test\", \"tet\")\nprint(f\"Distance between 'test' and 'tet': {result3}\")   # Expected: 1\n```\n\nThe function appears to be calculating distances incorrectly and may also throw IndexError exceptions in some cases when processing the strings."
